.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KEYEXCH_FREE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_fetch ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_free ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_up_ref ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_provider ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_is_a ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_do_all_provided ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_names_do_all ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_name ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_description ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_gettable_ctx_params ,
.Nm EVP_KEYEXCH_settable_ctx_params
.Nd Functions to manage EVP_KEYEXCH algorithm objects
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft EVP_KEYEXCH *
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_fetch
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *algorithm"
.Fa "const char *properties"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_free
.Fa "EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_up_ref
.Fa "EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_PROVIDER *
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_provider
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_is_a
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fa "const char *name"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_name
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_do_all_provided
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "void (*fn)(EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fa "void *arg)"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_names_do_all
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *exchange"
.Fa "void (*fn)(const char *name"
.Fa "void *data)"
.Fa "void *data"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_description
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *keyexch"
.Fc
.Ft const OSSL_PARAM *
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_gettable_ctx_params
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *keyexch"
.Fc
.Ft const OSSL_PARAM *
.Fo EVP_KEYEXCH_settable_ctx_params
.Fa "const EVP_KEYEXCH *keyexch"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_fetch
fetches the key exchange implementation for the given
.Fa algorithm
from any provider offering it, within the criteria given by the
.Fa properties .
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Pp
The returned value must eventually be freed with
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_free .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_free
decrements the reference count for the
.Vt EVP_KEYEXCH
structure.
Typically this structure will have been obtained from an earlier call to
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_fetch .
If the reference count drops to 0 then the structure is freed.
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_up_ref
increments the reference count for an
.Vt EVP_KEYEXCH
structure.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_provider
returns the provider that
.Fa exchange
was fetched from.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_is_a
checks if
.Fa exchange
is an implementation of an algorithm that's identifiable with
.Fa name .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_name
returns the algorithm name from the provided implementation for the
given
.Fa exchange .
Note that the
.Fa exchange
may have multiple synonyms associated with it.
In this case the first name from the algorithm definition is returned.
Ownership of the returned string is retained by the
.Fa exchange
object and should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_names_do_all
traverses all names for the
.Fa exchange ,
and calls
.Em fn
with each name and
.Fa data .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_get0_description
returns a description of the
.Fa keyexch ,
meant for display and human consumption.
The description is at the discretion of the
.Fa keyexch
implementation.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_do_all_provided
traverses all key exchange implementations by all activated providers in
the library context
.Fa libctx ,
and for each of the implementations, calls
.Em fn
with the implementation method and
.Fa data
as arguments.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_gettable_ctx_params
and
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_settable_ctx_params
return a constant
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array that describes the names and types of key parameters that can be
retrieved or set by a key exchange algorithm using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_get_params 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_fetch
returns a pointer to a
.Vt EVP_KEYEXCH
for success or NULL for failure.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_up_ref
returns 1 for success or 0 otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_names_do_all
returns 1 if the callback was called for all names.
A return value of 0 means that the callback was not called for any
names.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_is_a
returns 1 of
.Fa exchange
was identifiable, otherwise 0.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_gettable_ctx_params
and
.Fn EVP_KEYEXCH_settable_ctx_params
return a constant
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array or NULL on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER 3
.Sh HISTORY
The functions described here were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
